WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:07.350
There is a new poll about the virus which
shows that Republicans, Democrats and independents

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:12.070
are really living in alternate moral realities
when it comes to corona virus deaths.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.330
Now, notice that I'm not saying alternate
realities in this case.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.460
Everybody was presented with the fact that
at the time.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.759
One hundred and seventy six thousand people
had died of Corona virus.

00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:24.560
The poll was done a few days ago.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.119
We're now close to one hundred and eighty
one thousand coronavirus deaths.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.660
But at the time, Republicans, Democrats and
independents were told hundred and seventy

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.359
six thousand people have died of Corona virus.

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:36.359
Okay.

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:37.740
Presented with that fact.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.000
Do you believe that is an acceptable amount
of death?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.210
Most Republicans believe it is.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.210
Of course, Democrats and independents don't
think one hundred and seventy six thousand

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.280
deaths is acceptable.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:56.019
So this is a CBS News YouGov poll of twenty
two hundred registered voters.

00:00:56.019 --> 00:00:58.510
Margin of error of two point four.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:05.920
And it found that 57 percent of Republicans
believe 176 thousand Corona virus deaths is

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.920
acceptable.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.180
More than half of Republicans believe that's
an acceptable death toll.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:16.439
Only 10 percent of Democrats believe hundred
and seventy six thousand deaths is acceptable

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:20.880
and only 33 percent of independents do by
a two to one margin.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.049
Independents believe the death toll is unacceptable.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:26.820
Now, first of all, it's the hypocrisy.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:32.130
A ton of these same Republicans who say one
hundred seventy six thousand coronavirus deaths

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:38.500
are acceptable thought Barack Obama needed
to resign because two people died of Ebola

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.020
in the United States.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.890
There's always a hypocrisy angle.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.750
Let's not make that the focus today.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.930
Secondly, there is a morality component here.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:53.630
Is it possible that the reason Republicans
think the deaths are acceptable is that early

00:01:53.630 --> 00:02:01.369
on the deaths were mostly in blue states with
direct aviation links to China and the other

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:04.900
countries in Europe that were seeded with
the virus early?

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:11.080
Could it be that Republicans are okay with
deaths as long as they're mostly Democratic

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.080
voters?

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.430
I don't know the answer to that, but it's
certainly possible.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:21.020
But the really interesting thing statistically
is that you don't have an even partizan divide,

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.490
and that could be a factor in November.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.900
And I want to be really clear about explaining
this.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:32.520
We always expect that all else being equal,
if you have a purely partizan divide in any

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:39.480
issue, you would expect, for example, that
independents would be roughly 50/50 split

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:46.220
on an issue and you would expect that the
Democrat Republican imbalance would be equal.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.190
This isn't super clear the way I'm explaining
it.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.190
So.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.280
So let me give you an example.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:58.290
You would expect that if Republicans support
something, 70, 30 Democrats would oppose it.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.510
70, 30.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.560
All else being equal.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.440
Meaning if there isn't some other factor to
consider now, there's always some other factor

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.440
to consider.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.440
Right.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:11.640
So when you look at abortion, you don't have
approval for abortion in most cases among

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.640
Democrats.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.010
Equal to disapproval among Republicans.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.760
There's religious components.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.300
There's other factors that go into it.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.480
So right now, the country is more in favor
of abortion than they've ever been.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.360
And part of it is you don't have an even partizan
divide.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.080
Yes, Republicans are more against abortion
than Democrats, but it's not to the same degree.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.080
Okay.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.490
Here with this question on the acceptability
of corona virus deaths, the partizan divide

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.780
is very unequal.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.780
If we look at the.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:44.080
Numbers, again, you'll see that even among
Republicans, 43 percent think the death toll

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.080
is unacceptable.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:51.650
It is unbalanced with the Democratic number
showing us that this issue is stronger than

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:52.650
partizanship.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.700
It's still hugely partizan.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:04:00.720
But even Republicans, 43 percent of them,
are putting aside partizanship and saying

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.910
the death toll is not acceptable, despite
it being our guy Trump, who overside it's

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:07.910
not acceptable.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:14.210
And then, of course, when you look at independents
who are not 50/50 split, but by a two to one

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.900
margin, say this is not okay.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.769
This could be a difference maker in November.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:24.210
Coronaviruses polling as a top issue for voting
in November.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.319
And even among Republicans, 43 percent say
the results are unacceptable.

00:04:28.319 --> 00:04:33.419
If some of those Republicans vote Biden, if
some of them say, I'm not going to vote Biden,

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:34.800
but I'm going to stay home.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.849
It could be enough to push Trump out of office.

00:04:36.849 --> 00:04:39.850
Now, of course, on the other side, we've got
voter suppression.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.280
The Postal Service, foreign meddling.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.280
All of this stuff.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:50.360
So that's why we need to bring out in force
these folks who already Democrats by a 90

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.320
to 10 margin, think the coronavirus handling
is unacceptable.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.650
We've got to make sure that they vote.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:01.720
Last thing, how can Republicans call themselves
pro-life and be the group that by the largest

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:05.919
margin believes one hundred and seventy six
thousand deaths are acceptable?

00:05:05.919 --> 00:06:07.379
Just something to think about.

